  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">TB Supranational Reference Laboratory Network in Western and Central Africa - Africa - Multicountry TB WC Africa NTP/SRL (01-Jan-2019-31-Dec-2021)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Multicountry TB WC Africa NTP/SRL, Tuberculosis, National Tuberculosis Programme of the Republic of Benin (PNT)This program has the following goals: To build Tuberculosis (TB) Supranational Reference Laboratory (SRL) Network strengthening the capacity of National TB Reference laboratories to improve TB and MDR-TB diagnosis in Western and Central Africa. The objectives of this program are: To establish a regional National Tuberculosis Reference Laboratories (NTRLs) network in the West and Central African Region.  To support regional NTRL network with a centre-of-excellence for quality trainings, technical assistance and management systems.  To build technical capacity of prioritized NTRLs in national level disease monitoring surveys.  To strengthen the technical and administrative capacity of Supranational TB Reference Laboratory (SRL), Cotonou, Benin</narrative>
  </description>
